INT. SKATE-RINK SNACK BAR - AFTERNOON

Disco ball turning. Sticky floors. The smell of nacho cheese. Skates thump distantly on wooden floorboards beyond the glass.

PORTIA, 16, in a too-large varsity jacket, slumps at a corner table, chewing a straw. Across from her, KENJI, 17, bleach-tipped hair, rubs the brim of his cap between his fingers. LUPE, 15, ponytail, braces, bounces on the balls of her feet at the counter. ARCHIE, 16, in a hoodie, stands guard by the arcade machine, arms folded.

LUPE
Okay, okay, okay. She's coming.

KENJI
Who's coming?

LUPE
Mrs. Baptiste. With the clipboard.

PORTIA
Hide the trophy.

ARCHIE
What trophy?

PORTIA
The one in your jacket, genius.

ARCHIE
It's not in my jacket.

KENJI
It's sticking out of your jacket.

LUPE
Put it under the nachos.

ARCHIE
Under the nachos?

PORTIA
Under! The! Nachos!

Archie drops the little gold figurine into the cheese tray and covers it with a napkin. The four of them freeze as an adult shape appears behind the glass, walking slowly, scanning.

The shape passes. They exhale in unison. Kenji laughs, too loud. Portia kicks him under the table.

KENJI
Ow!

PORTIA
Sorry. Reflex.

LUPE
She didn't see.

ARCHIE
Of course she didn't. I'm a professional.

PORTIA
You are a thief.

ARCHIE
Borrower.

Behind the glass, the shape turns back. The four heads snap to the window. Archie, in a panic, digs the trophy out of the cheese and shoves it in his hood.

The shape keeps walking. Out the door. Gone.

For a moment nobody moves. Then Portia pulls the straw from her mouth and begins to laugh. Kenji joins. Lupe doubles over. Archie, holding a hood full of nacho cheese, lets his head fall back against the arcade cabinet.
